The Green Mile is a 1999 American fantasy drama film written and directed by
Frank Darabont and based on the 1996 novel by Stephen King.

12
02:06:00,000 --> 02:06:06,000
It stars Tom Hanks as a death row prison guard during the Great Depression who witnesses supernatural
events following the arrival of an enigmatic convict (Michael Clarke Duncan) at his facility.

13
02:16:30,000 --> 02:16:36,000
The Green Mile was released by Warner Bros.

14
02:27:00,000 --> 02:27:06,000
in the United States on December 10, 1999, to positive reviews from critics, who praised Darabont's direction and writing,
emotional weight, and performances (particularly for Hanks and Duncan), although its length received some criticism.

